     "notes": "Current flow 18,200 cubic feet per second.\r  \r  Water temp is 66\r \r Out draft conditions start at 32,000 cubic feet per second, \r \r In out draft conditions, two traveling mooring bitts will be used when pulling two or more lengths of loaded barges.\r \r Lock personnel will use the tow haulage unit to pull any combination of empty or loaded barges to a point just clearing the miter gates, provided that the section pulled does not have a lead notch adjacent to the guide wall in addition to any loaded barges abreast when flow are above 59,000 cfs. A helper boat can be utilized to hold the cut on the wall above 59,000 cfs. A notch with empties abreast will be allowed. Two traveling mooring bitts will be utilized, one traveling mooring bitt will be used from the bow barge quarter kevel and the other traveling mooring bitt will be used from the half or three-quarter kevel on the bow barge, requiring one extra line. One additional deck-hand will be required to handle lines on the section being pulled.",
